    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 offensive configuration today is anchored by **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) and **Gunnar Henderson** (69.90), who project as our premier daily assets. **Jackson Merrill** draws a favorable matchup against Trey Yesavage, benefiting from a 13% boost in SP skill projection and a solid platoon advantage. Meanwhile, **Gunnar Henderson** faces Noah Cameron in a venue providing a significant +16% park factor. Despite a slight penalty for Cameron\u2019s elite hold efficiency against base stealers, **Gunnar Henderson**\u2019s top-of-the-order role and power profile make him a near-lock for production. **Kyle Tucker** (69.76) and **Andy Pages** (65.76) round out the high-upside core; notably, **Andy Pages** receives a situational boost due to the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which increases his stolen base equity\u2014a critical metric for our roster construction.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the lineup optimizer involved **Miguel Vargas** (52.17), who narrowly missed the cut behind the more efficient floor provided by **Dominic Smith** and our middle infielders. While **Miguel Vargas** benefits from a strong xwOBA, the combination of an elite defensive catcher and high-efficiency hold SP suppressed his upside below the threshold. We are monitoring **Jorge Polanco** on the bench as well, though he remains sidelined today due to a 45% rain risk against Eduardo Rivera. As a general caution, note that all projections rely on pending lineups; should **Drake Baldwin** or **Liam Hicks** fall out of the top-four slots, their efficiency scores will likely shift as order-based multipliers are recalculated.",
